# CGGS Data Layer

## Pattern

```
UI Component → services/*.ts → public/mock-data/*.json
                              ↓ (future)
                         REST API
```

Never import JSON directly in pages or components.

## Service Example

```typescript
// src/services/events.ts
import type { SummitSchedule } from "@/types/events";

export async function getSchedule(): Promise<SummitSchedule> {
  const res = await fetch("/mock-data/events.json");
  return res.json();
}
```

## Types

Define interfaces in `src/types/` matching `03_DATA_MODELS.md`:

- `events.ts`, `speakers.ts`, `delegates.ts`, etc.

## Conventions

- IDs: `event_id`, `speaker_id`, `country_id`, `delegate_id`
- Dates: ISO format (`2027-02-15`)
- Times: 24-hour format (`09:30`)
- Mock JSON in `public/mock-data/` — human-readable, no duplicated data
- Structure responses like future REST payloads (wrap in `{ data: ... }` when appropriate)

## Mock Data Files

`events.json`, `speakers.json`, `fleet-review.json`, `countries.json`, `delegates.json`, `registration.json`, `accommodation.json`, `transport.json`, `notifications.json`, `gallery.json`, `news.json`, `downloads.json`
